  "step_2": "The individual in the verbal report states they reviewed the outcomes and decided on Lottery B because it offers a 100% chance of winning, whereas Lottery A has only a 99% chance. The individual explicitly compares the probabilities of receiving any positive outcome (i.e., 'Chance auf Gewinn') and uses this comparison as the justification for their choice. The focus is on the certainty of receiving a positive amount, not on the magnitude of the outcomes. The deliberation centers on the difference in likelihood between the two lotteries regarding obtaining a favorable (winning) result.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—comparing the probabilities of favorable outcomes between A and B—is directly considered by the individual, who notes the 100% vs. 99% chance of winning. The decision reason’s rule, which prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, aligns with the individual’s justification (choosing B due to higher certainty of winning). The verbal report mirrors both the informational focus and the decision rule of the reason. Therefore, it is certain that the individual used this decision reason.",
